  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "Heat 2 tablespoons of olive oil in a large pot. Add the chopped onion and diced carrots, lower the heat and sweat slowly until the carrot softens and the onion turns translucent. Meanwhile chop the remaining vegetables."
    },
    {
      "text": "Add the crushed garlic and fry for just a few seconds. Add the tomato paste and stir."
    },
    {
      "text": "Add the remaining vegetables and the white beans, cover with water (6 to 8 cups, depending on the size of the pot), add the bay leaf and thyme and salt generously."
    },
    {
      "text": "Bring to the boil, lower the heat and cook with the lid on for about an hour, until all the vegetables are soft. Taste and adjust the seasoning."
    }
  ]
